  "worked_solution": "An implication $A\u21d2B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent \"$7$ is divisible by $2$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent \"$8$ is divisible by $4$\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is divisible by $2$\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent \"$7$ is divisible by $4$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
